  "title": "BZR: Improve an infinite loop check",
  "description": "In some rare cases with unsigned offsets and lengths, the length does\nnot overflow but offset + length does overflow. Take a subset tvb\nto prevent this.\n\nAlso, get_bzr_prefixed_len, because it adds 4 to an unsigned, can\nreturn zero, so change some checks from \"length does not go backwards\"\nto \"length advances.\" This can't actually cause an infinite loop,\nbecause the length is advanced by 1 on the next iteration, but it\ncan give bogus results and should fail then.\n\nFix #21119\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
